  "_version": "1.0.0",
  "_description": "GitHub audit-log event → AKSI control ID mapping. GitHub's /orgs/{org}/audit-log endpoint and webhook events are THE evidence source for what code an AI coding agent (Claude Code, Cursor, Devin, Aider, etc.) actually produced — every push, PR, review comment, branch creation, secret rotation, and access-control change is recorded. Mapping is action-glob driven with overlays for branch_protection_evasion (admin override of branch protection — a critical compliance violation), bot/ML-powered actor detection (agent-authored work must be reviewed by a human), forked head_repository (untrusted source content), and role escalation (owner promotion). Cross-repo and bot-velocity patterns produce synthetic PR-02 FLAGs.",
